            {
                "entry_id": "d4325cad-1517-3614-90f5-b4b91a740953",
                "word": "clownerie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "54a70663-9ab5-459d-8601-0cbdbf509c06",
                        "entry_id": "d4325cad-1517-3614-90f5-b4b91a740953",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "clowneries"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1496dddc-0e03-3bd9-864a-a4a1258abe5e",
                        "entry_id": "d4325cad-1517-3614-90f5-b4b91a740953",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Farce ou tour de clown ou faisant penser à un clown."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d794ea2f-d80c-4109-8603-9cc1ff3b9458",
                                "sense_id": "1496dddc-0e03-3bd9-864a-a4a1258abe5e",
                                "text": "Un roman de ma vie ! Et moi qui avais toujours cru que la vie n’était pas un roman, – une clownerie, tout au plus !"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e8ce7562-ee51-485a-b310-9ae60656514f",
                                "sense_id": "1496dddc-0e03-3bd9-864a-a4a1258abe5e",
                                "text": "Il y a peu de choses nouvelles sous le soleil en matière de clowneries sociales. Aristote a déjà donné des règles de paix sociale ; […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "65a3d540-87e1-4e76-8d32-b48131f91344",
                                "sense_id": "1496dddc-0e03-3bd9-864a-a4a1258abe5e",
                                "text": "Le Paradis c’est le Larousse, on y est on y est pas, c’est de la clownerie à mourir."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "854cae31-7748-41c0-b3c5-4f0ac6a90c7c",
                                "sense_id": "1496dddc-0e03-3bd9-864a-a4a1258abe5e",
                                "text": "A ce titre notamment, la parodie n’est pas une farce, une sotie, une bouffonnerie ou une clownerie, qui sont des imitations réalisées dans le cadre d’un contexte régi par des conventions précises et limitées."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bf62da6c-843f-4586-9860-ebe02aa0ac86",
                        "source_entry_id": "d4325cad-1517-3614-90f5-b4b91a740953",
                        "source_sense_id": "1496dddc-0e03-3bd9-864a-a4a1258abe5e",
                        "target_lang_word": "clowning",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "clowning",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "da7fc0df-c92f-3eb6-bc16-48c737ce2d57",
                                        "entry_id": "b1d536cc-e057-3327-9dae-8b31b1352eae",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Clownish behavior."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "141d27f6-083f-483f-aff8-d7e0eb891ead",
                                                "sense_id": "da7fc0df-c92f-3eb6-bc16-48c737ce2d57",
                                                "text": "The press took seriously all Shaw's provocative ambiguities and clownings, and Lady Astor was identified with his most outrageous actions and statements."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "edc688e2-a25f-3ac9-8236-13b30dc9e1c4",
                                        "entry_id": "b1d536cc-e057-3327-9dae-8b31b1352eae",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The practice and study thereof."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ffdc8c1f-b316-46af-866c-fba75daa06f0",
                                                "sense_id": "edc688e2-a25f-3ac9-8236-13b30dc9e1c4",
                                                "text": "But it’s also a sign of the ascendant state of clowning, which, not long ago, resided in the bargain basement of artistic respect, alongside ventriloquists, mimes and jugglers. No longer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
